#: data_pivot_table_node.py:15
msgid "Creates a pivot table from a DataFrame. Specify row index columns, optional column index columns, value columns, and an aggregation function (mean, sum, count, min, or max)."
msgstr "Creates a pivot table from a DataFrame. Specify row index columns, optional column index columns, value columns, and an aggregation function (mean, sum, count, min, or max)."

#: data_eval_node.py:16
msgid "Evaluates a pandas eval expression on a DataFrame (e.g. 'C = A + B' to create a new column from arithmetic). Outputs the resulting DataFrame with the expression applied."
msgstr "Evaluates a pandas eval expression on a DataFrame (e.g. 'C = A + B' to create a new column from arithmetic). Outputs the resulting DataFrame with the expression applied."

#: data_export_node.py:22
msgid "Exports a DataFrame to a file in CSV, JSON, Excel, Parquet, or Feather format. Specify the output path and format; the output directory is created automatically if it does not exist."
msgstr "Exports a DataFrame to a file in CSV, JSON, Excel, Parquet, or Feather format. Specify the output path and format; the output directory is created automatically if it does not exist."

#: data_fill_interpolate_node.py:15
msgid "Fills missing values (NaN) by interpolation. Supports linear, polynomial, spline, and time-based interpolation methods."
msgstr "Fills missing values (NaN) by interpolation. Supports linear, polynomial, spline, and time-based interpolation methods."

#: data_fillna_node.py:15
msgid "Fills missing values (NaN) in a DataFrame using a specified method: constant value, forward fill, backward fill, mean, median, or mode."
msgstr "Fills missing values (NaN) in a DataFrame using a specified method: constant value, forward fill, backward fill, mean, median, or mode."

#: data_filter_by_column_node.py:15
msgid "Filters DataFrame rows by a numeric column's value range. Set min and/or max thresholds (inclusive); a value of 0 means no limit on that bound."
msgstr "Filters DataFrame rows by a numeric column's value range. Set min and/or max thresholds (inclusive); a value of 0 means no limit on that bound."

#: data_threshold_filter_node.py:15
msgid "Filters DataFrame rows by comparing a column's values against a threshold. Supports operators: >, >=, <, <=, ==, !=. Outputs the filtered data and the count of removed rows."
msgstr "Filters DataFrame rows by comparing a column's values against a threshold. Supports operators: >, >=, <, <=, ==, !=. Outputs the filtered data and the count of removed rows."

#: data_query_node.py:15
msgid "Filters DataFrame rows using a pandas query expression (e.g. 'age > 25 and name == \"John\"'). Outputs the filtered data and the result row count."
msgstr "Filters DataFrame rows using a pandas query expression (e.g. 'age > 25 and name == \"John\"'). Outputs the filtered data and the result row count."

#: data_filter_node.py:22
msgid "Filters DataFrame rows using a pandas query expression (e.g. 'age > 25') or by non-null values in a specified column. Outputs the filtered data and the count of removed rows."
msgstr "Filters DataFrame rows using a pandas query expression (e.g. 'age > 25') or by non-null values in a specified column. Outputs the filtered data and the count of removed rows."

#: data_plot_node.py:30
msgid "Generates a bar, line, or scatter chart from a DataFrame and saves it as a PNG image. Specify the target column and chart type; the file path is output for downstream use."
msgstr "Generates a bar, line, or scatter chart from a DataFrame and saves it as a PNG image. Specify the target column and chart type; the file path is output for downstream use."

#: data_describe_node.py:15
msgid "Generates descriptive statistics (count, mean, std, min, max, and configurable percentiles) for a DataFrame using pandas describe(). Outputs a statistics summary DataFrame."
msgstr "Generates descriptive statistics (count, mean, std, min, max, and configurable percentiles) for a DataFrame using pandas describe(). Outputs a statistics summary DataFrame."

#: data_source_node.py:23
msgid "Loads data from a file (CSV, Excel, JSON, or Parquet) into a DataFrame. Configure the file path and format; CSV supports encoding and separator options, Excel supports sheet selection."
msgstr "Loads data from a file (CSV, Excel, JSON, or Parquet) into a DataFrame. Configure the file path and format; CSV supports encoding and separator options, Excel supports sheet selection."

#: data_drop_duplicates_node.py:15
msgid "Removes duplicate rows from a DataFrame. Specify which columns to check for duplicates (comma-separated, empty = all columns) and whether to keep the first, last, or no duplicate occurrence."
msgstr "Removes duplicate rows from a DataFrame. Specify which columns to check for duplicates (comma-separated, empty = all columns) and whether to keep the first, last, or no duplicate occurrence."

#: data_remove_outliers_zscore_node.py:15
msgid "Removes outlier rows from a DataFrame using Z-score method. A row is removed if its Z-score (standard deviations from the mean) in the specified column exceeds the threshold (default 3.0)."
msgstr "Removes outlier rows from a DataFrame using Z-score method. A row is removed if its Z-score (standard deviations from the mean) in the specified column exceeds the threshold (default 3.0)."

#: data_remove_outliers_iqr_node.py:15
msgid "Removes outlier rows from a DataFrame using the IQR (interquartile range) method. Values outside 1.5×IQR (configurable) from the quartiles are treated as outliers and removed."
msgstr "Removes outlier rows from a DataFrame using the IQR (interquartile range) method. Values outside 1.5×IQR (configurable) from the quartiles are treated as outliers and removed."

#: data_dropna_node.py:16
msgid "Removes rows or columns containing missing values (NaN). Supports 'any' (drop if any value is missing) or 'all' (drop only if all values are missing) strategies, with optional column subset and minimum non-missing count threshold."
msgstr "Removes rows or columns containing missing values (NaN). Supports 'any' (drop if any value is missing) or 'all' (drop only if all values are missing) strategies, with optional column subset and minimum non-missing count threshold."

#: data_replace_values_node.py:15
msgid "Replaces a specific value with a new value in a selected column. Matching is case-sensitive. Outputs the modified DataFrame and the count of replacements made."
msgstr "Replaces a specific value with a new value in a selected column. Matching is case-sensitive. Outputs the modified DataFrame and the count of replacements made."

#: data_search_node.py:15
msgid "Searches a DataFrame for rows matching a pattern in a specified column. Supports regex patterns and case-sensitive matching. Outputs matching rows and the match count."
msgstr "Searches a DataFrame for rows matching a pattern in a specified column. Supports regex patterns and case-sensitive matching. Outputs matching rows and the match count."

#: data_sort_node.py:15
msgid "Sorts a DataFrame by one or more columns. Specify column names as a comma-separated list and choose ascending or descending order."
msgstr "Sorts a DataFrame by one or more columns. Specify column names as a comma-separated list and choose ascending or descending order."

#: data_transform_node.py:22
msgid "Transforms a DataFrame column: rename a column, drop a column, or fill missing values in a column. Specify the target column, operation type, and the corresponding parameter (new name or fill value)."
msgstr "Transforms a DataFrame column: rename a column, drop a column, or fill missing values in a column. Specify the target column, operation type, and the corresponding parameter (new name or fill value)."

#: data_query_node.py:20
msgid "query expression, e.g. 'age > 25 and name == \"John\"'"
msgstr "query expression, e.g. 'age > 25 and name == \"John\"'"
